    "lawCode": "Amd §§170.10 & 170.15, Pen L",
    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1897\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the penal law, in relation to including certain\ndocuments relating to ownership of a motor vehicle in the definition\nof a forged instrument\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to include an insurance card for a motor\nvehicle, a certificate of motor vehicle registration, and a title for\na motor vehicle in the list of items under forgery in the second\ndegree, when with intent to defraud, deceive or injure another, the\nperson falsely makes, completes or alters one of these written\ninstruments.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nA new subdivision 6 is added to section 170.10 of the Penal law to\ninclude an insurance card, certificate of registration or title\ndesignated for a motor vehicle in this section.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nExisting law does not include the aforementioned items under the\ndefinition of forgery in the second degree under Penal law section\n170.10 when persons use these items in a fraudulent manner.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis bill would add these documents to the list of items currently\ncontained in the Penal law section referring to forgery. The reason\nbehind the bill is to aid in deterring the ever growing problem of\nmotor vehicle theft. By adding these items to the list, it would add\nanother method of prosecution of individuals guilty of possessing a\nstolen vehicle.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n1996 - A11003 - referred to codes\n1998 - A4284  - held for consideration in codes\n2000 - A5347  - referred to codes\n2002 - A2083  - referred to codes\n2004 - A3137  - referred to codes\n2006 - S3294  - referred to codes\n2008 - S2280  - referred to codes\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the first of November next succeeding\nthe date it becomes law.\n",
